Found under k301 (2026-10-31). lib/OCP/Cmd/Destroy.pm (~line 517): when destroy finds no nodes, it prints "No nodes to destroy." and calls _cleanup_project_state, terminal or not and with no confirmation. That path came from k78 (state left behind after an out-of-band teardown). Since k301 the main path asks on a terminal or needs --force; this path removes the cluster's kubeconfig without either.

Provisional call (mine, the maintainer may override): ask the same way, through the k301 `_confirmed` (terminal or --force), before the cleanup. The question names what will be removed. `--keep_status` stays as it is. Reason: an empty node list can be stale or a read failure while the cluster is alive, and the kubeconfig is the way in.

Done = that, with tests for a terminal yes/no, a pipe, and --force, and k78's case still cleaned up with --force. Alternative, if the maintainer prefers: keep it unasked, but say on STDOUT exactly which files were removed.

